my/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/2bfda58fee727ccdc9f424140e2b8143bf5afe426ef0b1fa72105272d9a1b41e.png)\n\nAll other non-equilibrium solutions are parallel to the vector ${v}_{2}.$ So, the phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/f0821717299fb0b9858409db9a93a610a75e0564a2b60f5bfcd6eca26d2909ec.png)" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383177 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383178 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383179 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383180 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383181 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1041 "selection" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383181 13194139536090 true] [17592186383176 1110 #uuid "f6ffad53-b39e-533a-8c25-5fc7694782c4" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383177 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/dd3667299cd5da8fe5d9450799fbe865e832449ac39427795a5b87cf2786f587.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383177 1111 #uuid "22d84f7f-a204-591f-a881-eb61bea00810" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383178 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/8a7b634d05a938d9b481620da9837a8f28dc28f84ac18a3f9a20678ead0df20b.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383178 1111 #uuid "5376e69d-a7bc-5ac8-ade0-3f9d572db069" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383179 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/59b96e2396db2559e9893c73ef530a312a347442b9c4fde0137583310ceba0a9.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383179 1111 #uuid "844cd115-ce63-5e18-b11c-f93e3c496aff" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383180 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/f4b88938a280acb1149be29d6832483713437236424bbb640784a55bafea712c.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383180 1111 #uuid "23d3fe90-971e-545d-a2b7-2493f64a7768" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383181 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/f0821717299fb0b9858409db9a93a610a75e0564a2b60f5bfcd6eca26d2909ec.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383181 1111 #uuid "684cde0b-3a11-5003-a9c6-60c27e3fd2f9" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383183 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1089 "q-334638" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1100 "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-9x(t)+3y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ of the system's matrix $A$ is $v=[1,\\text{ }3]^{T}.$ The vector $w={[-\\frac{1}{3},\\text{ }0]}^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$  Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1113 #uuid "50bd4f72-f99e-562e-bd13-7cdd624e464a" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383182 1145 "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =0$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =0,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]t+[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that ${x}_{E}(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ are equilibrium solutions of the system since ${x}_{E}^{′}(t)=0.$ These solutions form the line with the equation $y=3x$ in the phase space, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/3a70188cf5de7e7b64530aa661447b7fa7fc1e918ca3de41088e67274d813b7a.png)\n\nNow, we consider some general solutions of the form \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}t-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFor example:\n\n- When ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=3,$ we get the following curve: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=9t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add it to the phase space:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/37deb5a0fda7ef15a016ec2d73a3b935074b6696184dd480ebe5b858ce517500.png)\n\n- When ${c}_{1}=-1$ and ${c}_{2}=-3,$ we get the following curve: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-3t \\\\ y=-9t-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's add it to the phase space:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/60b49680cf94888122f25432586a3546dea206ae960f951afd187444afc8881a.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/7b4de40b147f1745986476ab0b0cbad22ad0484924f62389c6c19187d5d06245.png)" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383184 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383185 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383186 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383187 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383188 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1041 "selection" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383187 13194139536090 true] [17592186383183 1110 #uuid "5350c3f6-c2cd-514b-a4f3-df186639d4c5" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383184 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/27610876df35c3b1e8e67e8958a5f28e26dfc26262e55994277629789a4bbd84.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383184 1111 #uuid "f6bd8fb6-6c17-526f-9aeb-f2d313fbc043" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383185 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/3aa0329f2b3017616c2010d4674c0dd13d9e277abe790e276a4e294087d6c685.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383185 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536090 true] [17592186383185 1111 #uuid "fcf07c60-9682-566e-ae07-9717c4294078" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383186 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14076166/assets/4a8d9528c878089370476a45aab127a416a11595ea0b0f972708e5161f208d5d.png" 13194139536090 true] [17592186383186 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 1319413953